  Interpretation:
    * 'agree-all'    = % of words where unconstrained cosine-argmax over all 15
                       canonicals matches the probe's top canonical. Chance = 1/15
                       ~= 6.7%.
    * 'agree-arity'  = same, restricted to canonicals of matching intended arity.
                       Chance = 1/n_intended_arity (1/8 ~= 12.5% for binary-intended;
                       1/7 ~= 14.3% for unary-intended).
    * 'arity-match'  = % of words where the unconstrained sim-all top has the same
                       ARITY as the probe's top canonical (ignores canonical identity).
                       Chance = max(7,8)/15 ~= 53.3% (the majority-arity baseline,
                       since with cosine-argmax over 15 canonicals the picked arity
                       has a slight bias toward the larger-arity class).

  If agree-arity is >= 60% per the §6 pre-spec threshold, the embedding-similarity
  heuristic explains the bulk of the probe's per-word routing once arity is
  controlled, and the §3.7.16 multi-factor mechanism reduces to 'softmax over
  arity-conditioned semantic neighborhood' at the focus layers. If it is at chance,
  the mechanism involves at least one factor not captured by mean-pooled-residual
  cosine (e.g., frequency-weighted softmax over the canonical readout vocabulary).

